WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
An FM radio station sends out radio waves.

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.290
In a hospital, X-rays are
used for medical imaging.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.730
One carries a station's broadcast.

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.820
The other lets doctors
see inside the body.

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:17.060
Two jobs, two names,
nothing obviously in common.

6
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.850
Are they one kind of wave, or two?

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.150
And what really tells them apart?

8
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.230
In this mission, you'll find out
what an electromagnetic wave is:

9
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.640
an oscillating electric field and an
oscillating magnetic field, moving together.

10
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.890
Then you'll see why such
a wave needs no medium,

11
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.780
and can cross a vacuum.

12
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.780
Your mission: decide whether X-rays
and radio waves are one kind of wave,

13
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:44.040
and find what really tells them apart.
